---
import Diagram from '../components/Diagram.astro';
import NextFocus from '../components/NextFocus.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { HERO } from '../lib/diagram';
import { PROFILE_SKILLS } from '../lib/profile-skills';
import { TRACKS, type Track } from '../lib/skill-tracks';

// A skill is trained now once the site measures it: its lessons, practice and review are there.
const now = (t: Track) => !PROFILE_SKILLS.find((s) => s.id === t.id)!.later;
const groups: { title: string; tracks: Track[] }[] = [
  { title: 'Train now', tracks: TRACKS.filter(now) },
  { title: 'Coming with later lessons, poker and the game-theory labs', tracks: TRACKS.filter((t) => !now(t)) },
];
const strength = ['Not trained', 'A little', 'Well', 'Strongly'];
---

<Base title="Chaalwise">
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div class="pitch">
      <h1>Strategy for people who run things, or are learning to.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        A strategy school that is always open. Learn to look ahead, weigh the odds, size a risk and keep a cool head, for work, for study and for life. Each
        idea is shown in a game, practised in a few minutes, and brought back until it sticks.
      </p>
      <NextFocus />
      <p class="terms">Free and offline. No account, no ads, and no money, ever.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="who">
      <h2>Who it is for</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>People who run teams and organisations.</strong> Plans, budgets, negotiations and hiring are strategy problems: what will the other side do,
          what can go wrong, how much to commit.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>People who want to succeed in one.</strong> Thinking a step ahead, and staying calm when a plan goes wrong, are what others notice.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Students.</strong> Exams, group projects and choices about what to study reward the same habits: check before you commit, and judge decisions,
          not results.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap map" id="skills" aria-labelledby="skills-title">
    <h2 id="skills-title">What you will get better at</h2>
    <p class="intro">
      Playing games on their own does little for general thinking. An idea is more likely to carry over when it is named, met in different settings and
      practised on your own decisions, so each strategy lesson shows where its idea turns up at work and in study, and asks you to use it. The games are the
      practice ground. The dots show how much each game exercises an idea, a judgement rather than a measurement: filled where you can practise it today, open
      where it is coming.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Skill, and where it pays off</th>
          <th scope="col">Chess</th>
          <th scope="col">Poker</th>
          <th scope="col">Also in</th>
          <th scope="col">
            <span class="sr-only">Where to train it</span>
          </th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      {groups.map((group) => (
        <tbody>
          <tr class="group">
            <th scope="colgroup" colspan="5">
              {group.title}
            </th>
          </tr>
          {group.tracks.map((track) => (
            <tr data-track={track.id}>
              <th scope="row">
                <a class="name" href={`/skills/${track.id}/`}>
                  {track.name}
                </a>
                <span class="life">{track.inLife}</span>
              </th>
              {(['chess', 'poker'] as const).map((game) => (
                <td class="dots" data-game={game === 'chess' ? 'Chess' : 'Poker'}>
                  <span class:list={['meter', game === 'chess' && now(track) ? 'now' : 'soon']} aria-hidden="true">
                    {[1, 2, 3].map((n) => (
                      <span class:list={{ on: track[game] >= n }} />
                    ))}
                  </span>
                  <span class="sr-only">
                    {strength[track[game]]}
                    {track[game] > 0 && (game === 'chess' && now(track) ? ', available now' : ', coming next')}
                  </span>
                </td>
              ))}
              <td class="also" data-game="Also in">
                {track.also || '–'}
              </td>
              <td class="go">{now(track) ? <a href={`/skills/${track.id}/`}>Train it</a> : <span>With {track.comesWith}</span>}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      ))}
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap steps" aria-labelledby="steps-title">
    <h2 id="steps-title">How a skill is trained</h2>
    <figure class="idea-board">
      <Diagram
        fen={HERO.fen}
        move={HERO.move}
        highlight={HERO.attacked}
        label="A chess position: White's knight jumps from d5 to c7, attacking Black's king on e8 and rook on a8 at once."
      />
      <figcaption>
        The blunder check, shown in chess: one knight move attacks the king and the rook together. At work it is the question before you send, sign or commit:
        what does this let the other side do?
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <h3>
          <a href="/skills/">Learn the idea</a>
        </h3>
        <p>A short lesson names the idea, shows why it matters, and where it turns up at work and in study.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>
          <a href="/reference/">See it in a game</a>
        </h3>
        <p>Chess now, poker next. Learn each game well enough to play it anywhere: its lessons, drills and terms are in the reference.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>
          <a href="/review/">Bring it back</a>
        </h3>
        <p>Each question comes back just before you would forget it, chess ideas in new positions.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>
          <a href="/progress/">Watch it settle</a>
        </h3>
        <p>Your skill profile, measured from your own answers and kept on this device.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    display: grid;
    gap: 32px 56px;
    align-items: center;
    padding-block: 32px 48px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 780px) {
    .hero {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      padding-block: 56px 72px;
    }
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5.6vw, 3.6rem);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 1.6vw, 1.3rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .terms {
    margin-top: 16px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .idea-board {
    margin: 0;
    width: min(100%, 360px);
  }
  figcaption {
    margin-top: 14px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  section + section,
  .map {
    margin-top: 56px;
  }
  .intro {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }

  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
  }
  thead th {
    text-align: left;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    padding: 0 12px 10px 0;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .group th {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 28px 0 8px;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  tbody tr[data-track] > * {
    padding: 14px 12px 14px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    vertical-align: middle;
    text-align: left;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  .name {
    display: block;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .life {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 2px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .meter {
    display: inline-flex;
    gap: 5px;
  }
  .meter span {
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--rule);
  }
  .now .on {
    background: var(--felt-2);
  }
  .soon .on {
    background: transparent;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--ink-2);
  }
  .also {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .go {
    white-space: nowrap;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .go span {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-weight: 400;
    white-space: normal;
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    thead {
      display: none;
    }
    table,
    tbody,
    tr,
    th,
    td {
      display: block;
    }
    tbody tr[data-track] {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: auto auto 1fr;
      gap: 6px 18px;
      padding: 14px 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    }
    tbody tr[data-track] > * {
      padding: 0;
      border: 0;
    }
    tbody tr[data-track] > th,
    .also,
    .go {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
    td[data-game]::before {
      content: attr(data-game) ' ';
      color: var(--ink-2);
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      margin-right: 6px;
    }
  }

  .steps {
    display: grid;
    gap: 24px 56px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  @media (min-width: 780px) {
    .steps {
      grid-template-columns: 360px minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
    .steps h2 {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
  }
  .steps ol {
    display: grid;
    gap: 24px 32px;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 230px), 1fr));
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: step;
  }
  .steps li {
    counter-increment: step;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
    padding-top: 14px;
  }
  .steps li::before {
    content: counter(step);
    display: block;
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    color: var(--felt-2);
  }
  .steps h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .steps p {
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .who h2 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .who ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .who li {
    padding-left: 16px;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
  }
  .who strong {
    display: block;
  }
</style>
